{% macro modules_section() %}
{% if has_modules %}
## Modules

{% for m in modules %}
- {{ m.label }} (`{{ m.id }}`){% if m.implied %} — implied dependency{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if has_files %}
### Files

Upload, list, metadata, download, and delete endpoints. Object bytes live in
{% if is_storage_local %}`STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT` (default `./var/storage`){% elif is_storage_s3 %}an S3-compatible bucket (`S3_*` settings){% else %}configured object storage{% endif %};
SQL stores metadata only (`storage_key` is a UUID-based opaque key).
{% if is_storage_s3 %}

The S3 bucket must already exist unless you set `S3_CREATE_BUCKET=true`
(opt-in; default is false).
{% endif %}
{% if has_minio %}

Start MinIO with Docker Compose (`minio` service), then point `S3_ENDPOINT_URL`
at it.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if has_background_jobs %}
### Background jobs

RQ workers read jobs from Redis (`REDIS_URL`). Start a worker with:

```bash
{{ worker_command }}
```

{% endif %}
{% if has_email %}
### Email

SMTP-backed `EmailService` (stdlib `smtplib`). Configure `SMTP_*` and
`EMAIL_FROM`. There is no public arbitrary-send HTTP endpoint — use the
service from application code (see tests for the injection pattern).
{% endif %}
{% if has_webhooks %}
### Webhooks

Outgoing delivery only: `deliver_webhook(payload)` enqueues an RQ job that
POSTs JSON to `WEBHOOK_URL` with timeout/`WEBHOOK_MAX_RETRIES`. No public
SSRF proxy endpoint.
{% endif %}

{% if has_products or has_categories or has_files %}
List and detail endpoints use page-number pagination where the framework supports it (page size 20).
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

